ruck was parked outside Telegraph Brewing Co on the Fourth of July. We tried a sampler platter to get a little of everything. Food was delicious. Ribs had a good flavor, the pulled pork was sweet and smoky and the chicken leg was nicely sauced. The sides were very generous sized. The coleslaw had a nice flavor and slight crunch and wasn't too wet or too sweet. The pinto (?) beans were awesome, esp with a splash of habanero sauce on them. And the mac and cheese had been grilled which did dry it out a hair but imparted a great taste that was worth the trade off. All in all it was delicious and a great value at $25.\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\",\"answer\":\"Here is an objective overview of AR Catering based on the provided structured data:\\n\\nAR Catering is a Mexican and barbecue restaurant located in Santa Barbara, California. They offer food delivery services and have a food truck, making them a convenient option for locals and visitors alike. Their menu includes a variety of dishes such as tacos, burritos, and BBQ favorites like ribs and pulled pork. They also offer catering services and event planning.\\n\\nAccording to customer reviews, the food at AR Catering is delicious and well-priced. One reviewer enjoyed the Sampler Platter, which included ribs, chicken, pulled pork, beans, garlic bread, and grilled mac n cheese. Another reviewer raved about the pork belly tacos, calling them \\\"absurdly good.\\\" A third reviewer appreciated the generous portion sizes and the variety of flavors offered on their menu.\\n\\nAR Catering has received positive reviews for their food and service, with an average rating of 4.5 stars out of 5. Customers have praised the restaurant for its delicious and authentic Mexican and barbecue dishes, as well as its convenient food delivery and catering services. Overall, AR Catering appears to be a great option for those looking for tasty and affordable Mexican and barbecue cuisine in Santa Barbara.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":