ead more.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how cardiovascular and digestive system are interrelated\\\"}\",\"answer\":\"The cardiovascular and digestive systems are interrelated in that the nutrients from digested food are absorbed into the bloodstream and transported to the rest of the body through the cardiovascular system. The cardiovascular system also plays a role in delivering oxygen to the digestive system to facilitate the breakdown of food. In return, the digestive system provides energy and nutrients to the body, which are then transported via the cardiovascular system to all the cells of the body, allowing them to function properly. Therefore, both systems are mutually dependent and work together to maintain homeostasis in the body.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":1138},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":1138,\"byte_end\":1152},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":1152,\"byte_end\":1656},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":1656,\"byte_end\":1745}],\"answer_sentence_indices\":[0,1,2,3],\"answer_offsets\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":208},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":208,\"byte_end\":334},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":334,\"byte_end\":532},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":532,\"byte_end\":633}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n"}
