3.36.951.614 D srv  log_server_r: request:  {"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "{\"instruction\":\"For each requested answer sentence emit index|E/C/B|p_unsupported with two decimals|[zero to two source segment indices]. One record per line in input order; no other text. Relations and addresses are predictions.\",\"source\":\"{\\\"passages\\\":\\\"passage 1:Communicable disease refers to diseases that can pass from one person to another. Non-communicable diseases occur in one person and cannot be passed on to another person. Communicable diseases are also known as infectious diseases, and non-communicable diseases are referred to as chronic.\\\\n\\\\npassage 2:One important difference between communicable and non-communicable disease is that non-communicable diseases tend to be chronic, which means they last a long time and progress slowly. Communicable diseases are more likely to be acute, which means the disease develops quickly.\\\\n\\\\npassage 3:Cancers are one category of non-communicable diseases that cannot be spread to others. Chicken pox and other conditions caused by viruses are communicable diseases. Non-infectious diseases involving the respiratory system are a class of non-communicable conditions.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"what is the difference between communicable and non communicable diseases\\\"}\",\"answer\":\"Communicable diseases can be passed from one person to another, while non-communicable diseases cannot be transmitted. Communicable diseases are often acute and caused by viruses, while non-communicable diseases are chronic and can last a long time. Some examples of communicable diseases are chicken pox, while non-communicable diseases include cancers and respiratory system conditions.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":105},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":105,\"byte_end\":194},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":194,\"byte_end\":510},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":510,\"byte_end\":703},{\"index\":4,\"byte_sta