28 of their 45 points in the second half after the game officials had pumped the balls back up to their proper pressure.\\n\\nIf the investigation finds that the Patriots did tamper with the footballs, they could face fines and/or the loss of a draft pick. In the past, the Patriots were punished for illegally videotaping opponents' signals during the 2007 \\\"Spygate\\\" scandal, which resulted in a first-round draft pick being taken away, a $250,000 fine for the team, and a $500,000 fine for Belichick.\\n\\nOther recent NFL rule violations have resulted in penalties for teams. The Cleveland Browns were fined $250,000 and their general manager suspended for four games for using electronic devices during games, and the Atlanta Falcons were fined $350,000 and lost a draft pick for playing artificial crowd noise in their stadium.\\n\\nThe outcome of the Deflategate investigation and the potential punishment for the Patriots is still unknown. NFL Commissioner Roger Goodell has stated that the league takes rule violations seriously and will address any wrongdoing in the investigation report.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":99},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":99,\"byte_end\":301},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":301,\"byte_end\":470},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":470,\"byte_end\":596},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":596,\"byte_end\":695},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":695,\"byte_end\":866},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":866,\"byte_end\":993},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":993,\"byte_end\":1213},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":1213,\"byte_end\":1320},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":1320,\"byte_end\":1411},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":1411,\"byte_end\":1635},{\"index\":11,\"byte_start\":1635,\"byte_end\":1830},{\"index\":12,\"byte_start\":1830,\"byte_end\":2127},{\"index\":13,\"byte_start\":2127,\"byte_end\":2232},{\"index\":14,\"byte_start\":2232,\"byte_end\":2363},{\"index\":15,\"byte_start\":2363,\"byte_end\":2491},{\"index\":16,\"byte_start\":2491,\"byte_end\":2684},{