ed tourists by helicopter, but the team was unable to land because of bad weather. Other rescue and relief operations in the region have faced similar weather issues. Crews planning to help those desperately in need are having to wait for storms to subside. Parajuli was told later that 23 people were rescued from the area and left on a bus headed for Kathmandu, but she wasn't sure if her father or his tour group were among them. \\\"All the people in the group are 60 years old or older. My dad said two Americans in the group were sick because of the weather and altitude, and since the people were older, they couldn't walk to help,\\\" she said. Now she is anxiously waiting for the weather to clear, and hoping to hear her father's voice again. If you are looking for someone, we invite you to share your story on CNN iReport. See scenes from Nepal after the earthquake. CNN's Sarah Brown and Anne Claire Stapleton contributed to this report.\\n\",\"answer\":\"Thousands of people remain missing in Nepal after a devastating earthquake struck the region on Saturday, including Nepalese, Indian, Chinese, and foreign tourists. Many families are using technology to search for their missing loved ones, sharing information on social media and online platforms. Some survivors have been reunited with their families, but many are still stranded and waiting for rescue. The walk of survival was a treacherous one for Raisaa Tashnova, a Bangladeshi woman who was on a group excursion near the Chinese border when the earthquake struck. She and her friends hiked for six hours through mountainous terrain to reach Kathmandu, where she was finally able to connect with her family. Dr. Carol Pineda and her husband, Michael MacDonald, were vacationing in Nepal when the quake hit, and their family was unable to locate them for several days. Eventually, they were able to send a voicemail to MacDonald's parents, indicating that they were safe but stranded. Janaki Parajuli, a Nepalese tour guide, was leading a group of senior citizens on a tour when the earthquake struck, and they were unable to contact anyone in the area. Parajuli's daughter, Jyotsna, received a call from her father explaining their situation, and she was able to help coordinate a rescue effort through the U.S. Embassy. However, the rescue team was unable to land due to bad weather, and Jyotsna remains anxious and hopeful for her father's safe return.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":96},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":96,\"byte_end\":267},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":267,\"byte_end\":396},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":396,\"byte_end\":514},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":514,\"byte_end\":660},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":660,\"byte_end\":891},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":891,\"byte_end\":913},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":913,\"byte_end\":1161},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":1161,\"byte_end\":1269},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":1269,\"byte_end\":1358},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":1358,\"byte_end\":1417},{\"index\":11,\"byte_start\":1417,\"byte_end\":1504},{\"index\":12,\"byte_start\":1504,\"byte_end\":1540},{\"index\":13,\"byte_start\":1540,\"byte_end\":1597},{\"index\":14,\"byte_start\":1597,\"byte_end\":1730},{\"index\":15,\"byte_start\":1730,\"byte_end\":1861},{\"index\":16,\"byte_start\":1861,\"byte_end\":1904},{\"index\":17,\"byte_start\":1904,\"byte_end\":1990},{\"index\":18,\"byte_start\":1990,\"byte_end\":2122},{\"index\":19,\"byte_start\":2122,\"byte_end\":2161},{\"index\":20,\"byte_start\":2161,\"byte_end\":2279},{\"index\":21,\"byte_start\":2279,\"byte_end\":2356},{\"index\":22,\"byte_start\":2356,\"byte_end\":2479},{\"index\":23,\"byte_start\":2479,\"byte_end\":2633},{\"index\":24,\"byte_start\":2633,\"byte_end\":2652},{\"index\":25,\"byte_start\":2652,\"byte_end\":2705},{\"index\":26,\"byte_start\":2705,\"byte_end\":2776},{\"index\":27,\"byte_start\":2776,\"byte_end\":2836},{\"index\":28,\"byte_start\":2836,\"byte_end\":2919},{\"index\":29,\"byte_start\":2919,\"byte