 hot before cooking. Yes you can use a regular cast iron pan. Start with high quality steaks, choice grade or better like a center cut, be it a filet, rib eye, or strip steak. With marbling, the white ribbons of fat running through the beef.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to cook flank steak indoors\\\"}\",\"answer\":\"Based on the given passages, here's how to cook flank steak indoors:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 250\u00b0F (200\u00b0C).\\n2. Season the flank steak with salt and pepper.\\n3. Place the steak on a rack over a baking sheet.\\n4. Roast the steak in the center of the oven for about 20 minutes, or until it reaches medium-rare.\\n5. Remove the steak from the oven and heat oil in a medium skillet over high heat.\\n6. Add the steak to the skillet and sear until it's deep brown and crisp, about 3 minutes per side.\\n7. Hold the steak on its sides and cook the edges for 1 minute per side.\\n8. Return the steak to the rack and let it rest for 10 minutes.\\n9. Slice the steak against the grain and serve.\\n\\nSo, the answer is: Preheat oven to 250\u00b0F, season the steak, place it on a rack, roast in the oven, sear in a skillet, and rest before slicing and serving.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":47},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":47,\"byte_end\":91},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":91,\"byte_end\":147},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":147,\"byte_end\":227},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":227,\"byte_end\":292},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":292,\"byte_end\":364},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":364,\"byte_end\":547},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":547,\"byte_end\":565},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":565,\"byte_end\":610},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":610,\"byte_end\":725},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":725,\"byte_end\":774},{\"index\":11,\"byte_start\":774,\"byte_end\":1016},{\"index\":12,\"byte_start\":1016,\"byte_end\":1090},{\"index\":13,\"byte_start\":1090,\"byte_end\":1139},{\"index\":14,\"byte_start\":1139,\"byte_end\":1319},{\"index\":15,\"byte_st